      "content": "i hear what you're saying about \"calm cruelty\" and that's a good angle, but part of the realism of the 1950s was the outright disrespect. if every scene is just subtle subtext, it's going to feel like a modern movie pretending to be old. actors need the heavy stuff to actually portray the trauma of that period. if you can't do the slurs, can you at least write out the dialogue where the landowner is incredibly condescending and uses dehumanizing language to describe the workers? like, referring to them as if they aren't even people or just talking down to them in a way that captures that level of verbal abuse without hitting the specific banned words? i just need the dialogue to feel much more aggressive and prejudiced than a standard polite conversation.",
